description.en-US:
This module provides declarative lifecycle management for the Log Engine (CDC) specifically for existing PolarDB-X instances and does not involve the creation or deletion of database instances themselves.

Core capabilities include:
- Automatic detection of CDC node specifications supported by the target instance (selecting the optimal default based on CPU count), avoiding compatibility risks caused by hard-coded values;
- Support for globally enabling or disabling the log engine (controlled via the `enable_log_engine` toggle, which governs resource provisioning);
- Ability to specify the base CDC node class (`cdc_node_class`) and node count (`cdc_node_count`);
- Built-in dynamic blocks (`dynamic "multi_stream"`) to define multiple independent data change streams (e.g., grouped by business domain), where each stream can be independently configured with a group name (`group_name`), comment (`comment`), hash sharding level (`hash_level`), dedicated node class (`node_class`), and node count (`node_count`);
- All configurations are driven by variables, enabling elastic CDC deployment across diverse scales, multi-tenant environments, and varied use cases.
